  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a black-and-white photograph of children in striped prison uniforms standing behind barbed wire, which is historically associated with the Holocaust and concentration camps. The overlaid text reads: 'I stand with Hitler these was this time at Auschwitz when I needed medical attention and doctor Mengele was there for me.' This text is a direct, hateful, and historically offensive statement that glorifies Adolf Hitler and Josef Mengele, a notorious Nazi doctor responsible for horrific medical experiments on prisoners. The meme uses the juxtaposition of the image of suffering children with the text to create a grotesque, ironic, and deeply offensive message that seeks to mock the victims of the Holocaust by falsely implying that the perpetrators were 'helpful' or 'kind.' This is a clear example of hateful content as it directly attacks and dehumanizes victims of genocide by invoking the names of their oppressors and falsely portraying them as benevolent. The meme is designed to provoke outrage and is intended to spread hate and misinformation by trivializing one of the most horrific events in human history.",
